rmally resolves its linker as the bare name `cc` and finds the SDK by running `xcrun` — both `PATH` lookups outside any fingerprinted tree, which decision 0008 §6 doesn't admit. Measured against 20 logging shims on `PATH`: with `SDKROOT` and `-Clinker=<root>/lib/rustlib/<target>/bin/rust-lld -Clinker-flavor=ld64.lld` pinned, both phases produced **zero** resolutions and a running Mach-O arm64 binary depending only on `libSystem`; the unpinned control resolved `xcrun` then `cc`. So the closure is `cargo → rustc → rust-lld`, three executables inside one fingerprinted distribution, with the SDK as a **data-only** second root. That avoids coining a sixth toolchain identifier — decision 0007's closed set is untouched and `toolchain_identities` stays at one element.\n\n**2. The pre-compile rejection matrix is computable.** `cargo metadata` ran a marker-writing `build.rs` and a marker-writing proc macro **zero** times (exit 0, neither marker written) while reporting `custom-build`, `proc-macro`, `links` and `source`. Without that, decision 0008 §7 would have disqualified the driver.\n\n## One correction upstream\n\nDecision 0007's expected `Cargo.toml` `rust-version` row moves from `compared` to `classified`: measured, the field has **three** host-independent acceptance layers (TOML type, grammar, edition floor) plus a separate host gate, pairwise independent. Unlike Go, isolation needs no harness surgery — `cargo metadata --no-deps` reports `rust_version` `1.99` on a 1.91.0 host with exit 0. Security partition is empty, so P1/P2 collapse to the satisfiable `C = Upstream`; both hold.\n\n## Honest limits\n\n- `platforms` holds **only** `(macos, arm64)`. macOS amd64, Windows and Linux are qualification obligations with a stated acceptance test — not claims. No Windows host had a Rust toolchain.\n- Two residual exposures are stated, not closed: compile-time `include!` reads (no sound pre-compile check exists, and **none of the six deferred hardened guarantees covers compile-time filesystem reads** — `STORY-260728-327soo` needs a seventh), and FFI against base-installation libraries.\n- A derive-heavy crate cannot be built by this driver. That's the accepted cost of rejecting proc macros outright.\n\n## Gates (real exit codes, run standalone)\n\nProbe `gofmt`/`vet`/`build`/`test` 0; probe runs 0 (`green: true` — 19/19 cases, 24 closure checks with 0 verdicts, 6/6 controls failing as required, 8/8 structural). Curator `go build`/`vet`/`test`/`gofmt` 0.\n\nTwo expected-red, both attributed: `make check` **2** (gofmt on four vendored files under another task's `.temp/` tree, zero from this task) and spec `validate.py` **1** (3 broken links, all inside two documents copied in from another task's in-flight tree pointing at rc.5 artifacts absent at the base commit — the clean-tree baseline at the same commit exits 0, and a scoped check over the two documents I authored reports 4 links, 0 broken). `golangci-lint` was **not run** — not installed on this host.\n\nNothing was staged, committed, pinned or published, and nothing was installed on any host.","ttft_ms":1568,"ttft_stream_ms":1056,"time_to_request_ms":16,"type":"result","duration_ms":2603219,"uuid":"a2a4892a-0fc9-4662-9622-fe794e9b80cb"}
